        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "60a2fb5c-41f6-5107-a2bb-808e86f21819",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Seasons: 1973–74 Houston Aeros season\n- Teams: Houston Aeros, Detroit Red Wings\n- Leagues: World Hockey Association\n- People: Gordie Howe, Sid Abel, Ted Lindsay\n- Concepts: Production Line\n- Organizations: Hockey Hall of Fame\n\nFacts:\n- The 1973–74 Houston Aeros season was the Houston Aeros' second season of operation in the World Hockey Association.\n- The 1973–74 Houston Aeros season saw the debut of Gordie Howe and his sons in the World Hockey Association.\n- Gordie Howe was nicknamed \"Mr. Hockey\" and is considered one of the greatest ice hockey players of all time.\n- The Production Line was the Detroit Red Wings line of Gordie Howe at right wing, Sid Abel at centre, and Ted Lindsay at left wing.\n- Gordie Howe, Sid Abel, and Ted Lindsay were all members of the Hockey Hall of Fame.",
